   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualification to hold\nthe position of assistant district attorney in the county of Rockland",
    "basePrintNo": "S8545",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8545-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8545\n\nSPONSOR: REICHLIN-MELNICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualification to\nhold the position of assistant district attorney in the county of Rock-\nland\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo amend the law to allow residents of Rockland County and adjoining\ncounties to serve as assistant district attorneys in Rockland County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one adds subdivision 72 to section 3 of the public officers law,\nallowing residents of counties which adjoin Rockland County to serve as\nassistant district attorneys in Rockland County. This provision does not\napply to the position of chief assistant district attorney.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill was introduced at the request of the Rockland County District\nAttorney's Office. The Rockland County DA's office is in need of quali-\nfied persons to serve as assistant district attorneys.  This act will\ngive Rockland County the same level of flexibility already afforded to\nso many counties by allowing the DA to hire qualified lawyers who live\nin the counties which adjoin Rockland County.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
